    "ExplanationWrongA": "$375,000 is the breakeven point: $150,000 ÷ 0.40 = $375,000. This covers fixed costs only and leaves no room for the $50,000 target profit. A candidate reaching this answer has correctly applied the CM ratio but omitted the target profit from the numerator. Both amounts must be grossed up together: ($150,000 + $50,000) ÷ 0.40 = $500,000.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "",
