    "ExplanationCorrect": "The newsvendor model orders the quantity that balances the cost of understocking against the cost of overstocking. Cost of underage Cu = $75 − $35 = $40 (profit lost on each unit of demand that cannot be served). Cost of overage Co = $35 − $20 = $15 (loss on each unit that must be salvaged). The critical ratio is Cu ÷ (Cu + Co) = $40 ÷ $55 = 0.727 — the optimal service level. With normal demand μ = 500 and σ = 100, the z-score corresponding to 0.727 is approximately 0.60. Order quantity = μ + zσ = 500 + 0.60(100) = 560 units. FreshFarm should order 560 units. A common error is ordering the mean (ignoring the asymmetry — underage is far more costly than overage) or plugging the ratio itself in as the z-score.",
