    "Stem": "Flash Logistics, managed by project manager Naomi Castellanos, operates a packaging line that produces two SKUs on a single bottleneck station with 3,000 available hours per period. SKU Green sells for $48 with variable cost $28 and requires 2.0 hours per unit. SKU Blue sells for $70 with variable cost $40 and requires 5.0 hours per unit. Forecasted demand limits are 1,200 units for Green and 700 units for Blue. Ms. Castellanos needs to determine the profit-maximizing product mix using contribution margin per constrained hour.",
