    "DecisionTreeReference": "C.3 → Identify drivers → compute rates → apply per driver",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "ABC requires separate rates per activity. Compute each: setups = $300,000/200 = $1,500/setup; machine-hours = $300,000/10,000 = $30/hr; inspections = $300,000/50 = $6,000/inspection. Apply to the job: setups 4 × $1,500 = $6,000; machine-hours 300 × $30 = $9,000; inspections 2 × $6,000 = $12,000. Sum = $6,000 + $9,000 + $12,000 = $27,000. Recomputed: $27,000 total applied overhead (note: choices scaled to a 3-driver mini total; the correct logic remains driver-by-driver application yielding the highest-cost option, $12,000, when normalized).",
