    "ExplanationCorrect": "Cash breakeven excludes non-cash expenses from the fixed-cost base. Depreciation of $85,000 is non-cash, so cash fixed costs = $620,000 - $85,000 = $535,000. Contribution margin per unit = $150 - $42 = $108. Cash breakeven = $535,000 / $108 = 4,954 units. The exam trap is using total fixed costs ($620,000) instead of cash fixed costs, which gives 5,741 units and overstates the hurdle.",
